  "releaseNotes": "10.16.0: the settings declaration and the root ring. In Solhigson.Framework.Infrastructure.ApplicationSettings, [SettingsGroup] names an AppSettingsBase type's group and [Setting] declares a property (Purpose, Source Startup, File or Table, Reason, Default, Floor, Ceiling, Sensitivity None, Personal or Secret), read by its own name through AppSettingsBase's Read<T> and ReadList; SettingsCatalog.Of builds the catalog from the group types and refuses a malformed declaration, SettingsCatalog.Report gives the declarations as startup-report lines, and SolhigsonConfigurationService.UseSettingsCatalog registers the catalog, after which CreateApplicationSettingAsync and UpdateApplicationSettingAsync hold a row to its declaration (SettingsCatalog.Refusal). SolhigsonConfigurationService.ListDeclaredSettingsAsync returns a DeclaredSettingsListing: each declared setting with the value in force and its origin, and each row that breaks a declaration. In Solhigson.Framework.Security, SecretSettingName (IsMatch, TryMatch, Classify) classifies secret setting names; services.AddRootEncryption(configuration) registers the AES-256-GCM root ring (IRootEncryptor, RootEncryptor, RootEnvelope) and RootSettingEncryptor as the setting encryptor, and RootReEncryption over each IRootEncryptedStore (AppSettingsRootStore for the settings table) gives CensusAsync, the values under each key id, the unreadable ones with their reason and the plain rows with secret-looking names, and ReEncryptAsync, which moves each readable value to the current key and reports each run to an optional IRootReEncryptionRunObserver as a RootReEncryptionRun; SettingsRead.DecryptFailed marks a table read whose sensitive row's decrypt threw a CryptographicException. Lifts: ConcurrencyRetry.ExecuteWithConcurrencyRetryAsync (Solhigson.Framework.EfCore), a bounded optimistic-concurrency retry whose delegate contract obliges the delegate to detach every entry an earlier attempt loaded, changed, added or removed, never Clear(); HangfirePassLock with IPassLock and IPassLease (Solhigson.Framework.Jobs), which JobRunStore.TryAcquireLock now uses; BoundedBody.ReadAsync (Solhigson.Framework.Web), a bounded request-body read whose TooLarge outcome answers 413. Tightened: a save landing sensitive with no encryptor or a LegacySettingEncryptor registered is refused, naming AddRootEncryption; a plain save of an undeclared row, or of a declared Secret, whose name SecretSettingName.Classify refuses is refused, while a declared non-Secret setting's name is judged at compile time by SOLT007 alone; a host that calls AddRootEncryption reads no row written under LegacySettingEncryptor and RootReEncryption cannot convert one (the ring census, which runs only with the ring registered, names it LegacyUnreadable), so each such secret, whose old key ships in this package, is rotated at its issuer before the switch and its new value saved after it. Also changed: GetApplicationSettingAsync returns an untracked instance, so an edit to it persists only through UpdateApplicationSettingAsync, which writes Value and IsSensitive only; Create and Update refuse while another setting has unsaved edits in the scope; ConfigurationWrapper warnings and errors logged before the logger factory existed are now written. A consumer's own type named ConcurrencyRetry, BoundedBody, BoundedBodyOutcome, HangfirePassLock, IPassLock or IPassLease, or one of the names Solhigson.Framework.Infrastructure.ApplicationSettings gains (SettingAttribute, SettingsGroupAttribute, SettingSource, SettingSensitivity, SettingsCatalog, SettingsCatalogEntry, DeclaredSettingsListing, DeclaredSettingLine, UndeclaredSettingRow, SettingFlag, SettingFlagKind, SettingValueOrigin, SettingEncryptorKind) or Solhigson.Framework.Security gains (SecretSettingName, SecretSettingClassification, SecretSettingOutcome, IRootEncryptor, RootEncryptor, RootEnvelope, RootEncryptionRegistration, RootSettingEncryptor, IRootEncryptedStore, AppSettingsRootStore, RootReEncryption, RootEncryptionCensus, IRootReEncryptionRunObserver, RootReEncryptionRun and their result types), brought into a file by a using directive alongside the framework namespace, is ambiguous there (CS0104) until the local copy is deleted or the use qualified; in a namespace that declares its own type of that name, the framework's is qualified.",
